  "report": "This report is for educational use only and is not financial advice. MCP returned a successful FCFF valuation for NVIDIA Corporation in USD, with estimated value per share of 424.19 and market price of 215.33. Growth is the central driver: revenue growth is modeled at 28.64% for years 2-5, then fades over the projection period toward a 4.6% terminal growth rate; the semiconductor growth anchor shows a 2026 median proxy near 12.86% with 0.778 confidence. Margins begin from very high profitability: next-year operating margin is 75.0%, converging toward a 55.76% target margin. Reinvestment is represented through sales-to-capital: 1.99x in years 1-5 and 1.10x in years 6-10, so the model requires substantial reinvestment to support projected revenue scale. Cost of capital starts at 10.05% and fades to 9.63% terminal cost of capital, using a 4.6% risk-free rate and configured Damodaran equity risk premium inputs. Terminal value is large in the output: terminal cash flow is 1.102 trillion, terminal value is 21.902 trillion, and present value of terminal value is 5.297 trillion, making the result sensitive to terminal assumptions. Data caveats: MCP warns that rates are percentages, sales-to-capital is a multiple, expectation checks solve one variable at a time, and Yahoo Finance coverage can be missing, stale, or insufficient for some companies."
